meta {
  name: 11. Unrelease DataSet (triggers delete saga)
  type: http
  seq: 33
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:id/unrelease
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{sagaDataSetId}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // The preceding toggle UPDATE sagas (9f/9h) must fully settle (pendingSagaType null) before we can
  // unrelease, else the backend returns 409 (a saga is already in flight); 9i/9j/10 are read-only and
  // don't wait. With two named APIs (STA + OWS) those sagas provision/re-apply two routes, so settling
  // takes a bit longer — poll until settled (deterministic, not a fixed sleep). Same pattern (and
  // QuickJS token boilerplate) as 9f/9h.
  const axios = require('axios');
  const base = bru.getEnvVar('baseUrl');
  const kc = bru.getEnvVar('keycloakUrl');
  const realm = bru.getEnvVar('realm');
  const id = bru.getVar('sagaDataSetId');

  const form =
    'grant_type=password' +
    '&client_id=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('clientId')) +
    '&client_secret=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('clientSecret')) +
    '&username=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('username')) +
    '&password=' + encodeURIComponent(bru.getEnvVar('password'));

  // Fail loudly if readiness can't be proven — otherwise we'd POST the unrelease while the previous
  // saga is still active and hit the very 409 race this guard exists to remove.
  let bearer = '';
  try {
    const tok = await axios.post(`${kc}/realms/${realm}/protocol/openid-connect/token`, form, {
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
    });
    bearer = tok.data && tok.data.access_token;
  } catch (e) {
    throw new Error(`Settle-check token fetch failed: ${e.message}`);
  }
  if (!bearer) {
    throw new Error('Settle-check token fetch returned no access_token');
  }

  let settled = false;
  for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) {
    let pending = 'unknown'; // sentinel: a failed read stays "not settled", never breaks the loop
    try {
      const r = await axios.get(`${base}/datasets/${id}`, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${bearer}` } });
      pending = r.data.pendingSagaType;
    } catch (e) { /* transient; retry */ }
    if (pending === null || pending === undefined) { settled = true; break; }
    await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, 2000));
  }
  if (!settled) {
    throw new Error('Dataset did not settle (pendingSagaType still set) — refusing to unrelease during an active saga');
  }
}

tests {
  test("Unrelease accepted — DELETE saga triggered (exactly 202)", function() {
    // The precondition guarantees an AVAILABLE, settled dataset (pre-request polled pendingSagaType
    // to null), so the unrelease MUST be accepted with 202. A 400 means the dataset was not in
    // AVAILABLE state — i.e. the DELETE saga did NOT start — which would silently invalidate the
    // downstream cleanup checks (11b). Accepting it here would mask that state error. (A genuine
    // not-AVAILABLE rejection belongs in a dedicated sad-path test, not the happy path.)
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(202);
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 11 of 18** — Trigger the DATASET_DELETE saga (cleanup phase).

  Transitions the dataset from `AVAILABLE` back to `READY` and triggers the **DATASET_DELETE** saga asynchronously. The saga de-provisions infrastructure in reverse order:

  1. **Pipeline engine** — removes deployed pipelines
  2. **APISIX Gateway** — removes all named-API routes + the dataset's upstream
  3. **FROST Server** — removes the Project

  On completion, the dataset reverts to `READY` state and `pendingSagaType` becomes `null`.

  **Precondition:** `sagaDataSetId` is set; dataset is in `AVAILABLE` state.

  **Expected Response:** 202 Accepted (saga triggered). 400 if the dataset is not in `AVAILABLE` state.

  **Kafka Events**
  - Produces: `de.civitascore.dataset.saga.trigger` (sagaType: `DATASET_DELETE`)
  - Consumes: `de.civitascore.saga.result` (type: `SAGA_COMPLETED` or `SAGA_FAILED`)

  **System Impact:**

  | System | Expected Change |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | DataSet status → `READY`; `pendingSagaType` set to `DELETE` until saga completes |
  | Config Adapter (Orchestrator) | Receives saga trigger; de-provisions pipeline engine → APISIX → FROST in reverse |
  | FROST Server | Project removed |
  | APISIX Gateway | Route + upstream removed |
  | Pipeline engine | Pipelines undeployed |
}
